WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.083 --> 00:00:04.083
Gentlemen.

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:08.792
All right, E Streeters!

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:09.958
Let's do this thing.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.542
We're, uh, sitting at Thrill Hill Recording in

00:00:14.542 --> 00:00:16.292
the wilds of New Jersey

00:00:16.292 --> 00:00:18.625
having reconvened the E Street Band.

00:00:18.958 --> 00:00:21.292
When you get back together it's just a power

00:00:21.292 --> 00:00:22.750
it's like a family reuniting.

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:25.208
Real friends for forty-years

00:00:25.208 --> 00:00:27.292
all contributing something artistically.

00:00:27.292 --> 00:00:28.792
That's something special.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:32.083
The greatest thrill in my life is

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.292
standing behind that microphone

00:00:34.292 --> 00:00:35.542
with you guys behind me.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:36.458
Let's do it.

00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:40.958
There's, uh, a terrific, unspoken,

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.375
kind of affinity

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.792
for what we're about to do.

00:00:43.792 --> 00:00:45.792
♪♪

00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:46.667
We showed up

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:48.500
with no demos sent

00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:51.167
no chance to write out charts and get to know the songs.

00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:53.833
The way we do things,

00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:55.917
capturing the excitement while it's happening.

00:00:55.958 --> 00:00:57.667
The only other time we worked this way

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.042
would be Born In The U.S.A.

00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:03.042
When we play together, it's 1977

00:01:03.042 --> 00:01:04.083
all over again.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.750
It's all about the songs, right?

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.125
And the inspiration for those songs

00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:09.292
comes from what I know

00:01:09.292 --> 00:01:10.667
you guys are gonna be playing.

00:01:11.059 --> 00:01:14.474
♪♪

00:01:15.292 --> 00:01:17.792
You're not exactly sure where you're going.

00:01:17.792 --> 00:01:20.500
But, you know if you jump onto his energy,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:21.917
and his direction

00:01:21.917 --> 00:01:23.125
you'll get there together.

00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:27.000
You're holding on to just learn the basic song

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.375
and then even Bruce is kind of

00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:30.000
changing his mind about things.

00:01:30.458 --> 00:01:32.292
Don't play it up higher, just don't play so low.

00:01:34.441 --> 00:01:35.958
♪♪

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:36.958
But invariably...

00:01:36.958 --> 00:01:38.167
Let's get the claps

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.500
and get the la da da's.

00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:40.958
...it will trigger an idea.

00:01:40.958 --> 00:01:44.625
♪♪

00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:46.583
It's just gotten better, blows my mind.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.583
Bruce is one of the great songwriters in history.

00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:55.208
♪♪

00:01:55.208 --> 00:01:57.583
It's the journey not so much the destination.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.417
And him recognizing that

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:00.625
is why he's a great artist.

00:02:00.956 --> 00:02:04.958
♪♪

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.917
There's a moment where it all comes together, and it's fleeting.

00:02:07.917 --> 00:02:09.625
♪♪

00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:12.000
I've heard it described as catching lightning in a bottle.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.750
And that's catching the magic.

00:02:15.627 --> 00:02:22.525
♪♪

00:02:24.792 --> 00:02:25.375
Perfect!

00:02:25.458 --> 00:02:26.417
Perfect!

